Let’s clearly understand Offset Pagination vs Cursor Pagination.

1️⃣ Offset Pagination
📌 What it is

Uses LIMIT and OFFSET in SQL.

SELECT *
FROM users
ORDER BY id
LIMIT 10 OFFSET 20;

👉 This means:

Skip first 20 rows

Return next 10 rows

📌 How it works

If:

Page size = 10

Page number = 3

Then:

OFFSET = (pageNumber - 1) * pageSize
OFFSET = (3 - 1) * 10 = 20
📌 Example

Page 1:

LIMIT 10 OFFSET 0

Page 2:

LIMIT 10 OFFSET 10

Page 3:

LIMIT 10 OFFSET 20
📌 Advantages

✅ Simple to implement
✅ Easy to understand
✅ Allows jumping directly to page 50

📌 Problems

❌ Slow for large datasets

If OFFSET = 1,000,000
Database still scans first 1,000,000 rows and discards them.

❌ Data inconsistency

If someone inserts a record while paging:

You may see duplicate data

Or miss some records

2️⃣ Cursor Pagination (Keyset Pagination)
📌 What it is

Instead of OFFSET, we use a reference column (cursor) like id, created_at.

SELECT *
FROM users
WHERE id > 20
ORDER BY id
LIMIT 10;

Here:

20 is the last id from previous page

This is called the cursor

📌 How it works

Page 1:

SELECT * FROM users
ORDER BY id
LIMIT 10;

Last id returned = 10

Page 2:

SELECT * FROM users
WHERE id > 10
ORDER BY id
LIMIT 10;

Page 3:

WHERE id > 20
📌 Advantages

✅ Much faster for large datasets
✅ Uses index properly
✅ No skipping/scanning millions of rows
✅ More consistent with inserts

📌 Limitations

❌ Cannot jump directly to page 50
❌ Needs a stable, indexed column (like id or created_at)
❌ Slightly more complex implementation

🔥 Performance Comparison
| Feature                | Offset Pagination | Cursor Pagination |
| ---------------------- | ----------------- | ----------------- |
| Large data performance | ❌ Slow            | ✅ Fast            |
| Jump to any page       | ✅ Yes             | ❌ No              |
| Handles inserts well   | ❌ No              | ✅ Yes             |
| Implementation         | Easy              | Medium            |

🎯 When to Use What?
✅ Use Offset Pagination When:

Small dataset

Admin panel

Need direct page navigation

✅ Use Cursor Pagination When:

Large dataset

Infinite scroll

APIs

Social media feeds

High performance systems

💡 Real World Example

Instagram, Twitter → Cursor pagination

Admin dashboards → Offset pagination

🚀 Interview Answer (Short Version)

If interviewer asks:

What is difference between offset and cursor pagination?

You can say:

Offset pagination uses LIMIT and OFFSET and is easy but slow for large datasets because database scans skipped rows.
Cursor pagination uses a reference column like id and is more efficient and consistent for large datasets, but does not allow direct page jumping.